📅 Day 53 – JSTL & JavaBeans in JSP

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on JSTL (JavaServer Pages Standard Tag Library) and JavaBeans, which help in writing clean and maintainable JSP code without embedding Java logic directly.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ JSTL (JavaServer Pages Standard Tag Library)
JSTL provides predefined tags to perform common operations
Reduces the need for Java code in JSP
Makes code cleaner and more readable
Common JSTL Tags:
<c:forEach> → Looping
<c:if> → Conditional statements
<c:out> → Display output
2️⃣ JavaBeans
JavaBeans are simple Java classes used to store data
Follow standard conventions:
Private variables
Public getter and setter methods
Used to transfer data between JSP and backend
🔹 Advantages
Cleaner code (no scriptlets)
Better separation of logic and presentation
Improved maintainability
🔹 Practical Work

During the practice session, I:

Used JSTL tags for looping and condition checking
Created JavaBeans to store and manage data
Integrated JavaBeans with JSP pages
Reduced use of scriptlets for cleaner code